Famouskai syntax sample: diff (ace/mode/diff)
The same small project, the Word Count tool, compared in four diff formats.
The Preview button renders the two unified sections side by side; it does not show the other two formats.
Lines before the first header are ignored by patch tools, so they can explain the change.
Every hunk below was produced by git or GNU diff, then checked with "git apply --check" or "patch --dry-run" (the binary line has no content to apply).

﹥ 1. Unified format, Subversion style (Index line, revisions instead of a/ and b/)
Index: README.md
===================================================================
--- README.md	(revision 41)
+++ README.md	(working copy)
@@ -1,7 +1,10 @@
 # Word Count tool
 
-A Famouskai tool that counts the words of the open file.
+A Famouskai tool that counts the words of the open file, in any language.
 
 ## Install
 
-Copy `plugins/tool-word-count.js` into your Famouskai `plugins/` folder.
+1. Copy `plugins/tool-word-count.js` into your Famouskai `plugins/` folder.
+2. Add it to the list of files in `sw.js`, so it works offline.
+
+See [the guide](docs/guide.md).

